PUT YOUR STATION PHOTOS IN THIS FOLDER
======================================

Walk the Line will show a real photo at the top of each person's chat if you
put one here. If a photo is missing, it just shows the built-in drawing instead
— so you can add them one at a time, in any order, and nothing breaks.

HOW
---
1. Get a photo for a station (a real shop photo, or an AI-generated one like
   your collage). Landscape works best — roughly twice as wide as it is tall.
2. Name the file exactly after the station, all lowercase:

       cut.jpg     -> Cutting (Dave)
       parts.jpg   -> Small parts (Priya)
       store.jpg   -> Laydown / storage (Tom)
       panel.jpg   -> Panel fab (Sam)
       stiff.jpg   -> Stiffener mounting (Jack)
       sub.jpg     -> Sub-assembly (Maria)
       unit.jpg    -> Unit line (Nadia)

   .jpg, .jpeg, .png and .webp all work — just keep the name (cut, parts, …)
   the same.

3. Put the file in this "line-images" folder, next to index.html.
   If you're on GitHub: open this folder, "Add file" -> "Upload files",
   drop the photo in, commit.

4. Reopen the app and tap that person — you'll see the photo.

TIPS
----
- Keep each photo under ~500 KB so the app stays quick to load. Most phone
  photos are fine once resized; if one is huge, shrink it first.
- Don't upload anything commercially sensitive if the repo is public. If in
  doubt, keep the repo private, or use generic/AI images.
- To go back to the drawing for a station, just delete its photo here.
